From f31782a74432e2c5af9723fba8a22bfdad5ab0d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:38:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: sample packed depth as depth, stencil blits
 on the CPU

- Z24_UNORM_S8_UINT sampled as an integer: on big endian its first
  non-void channel is the stencil, which set NUM_FORMAT_INT, so sampled
  depth saturated to 1.0. The depth channel decides for depth formats.
  Fixes depth blits, copies and depth textures of packed depth/stencil.
- Stencil blits: Xenos has no stencil export and no integer sampling, so
  u_blitter's per-bit fallback can't read the source. Copy the stencil
  bytes on the CPU through the (converting) transfers, after the GPU part
  of a depth+stencil blit.

